1. Purpose and relationship to the main licence

The teamknitt software is offered under the Teamknitt Noncommercial and Research
Licence 2.0 (the "Main Licence"), in the LICENSE file at the root of the
teamknitt repository. The Main Licence limits free use to noncommercial use and
to qualifying academic research.

This Skill Licence is a separate, additional permission from the licensor. It
lets anyone use the unmodified teamknitt skill in Claude, for any purpose,
without meeting the noncommercial, research, institutional or geographic
conditions of the Main Licence. It applies only to Skill Use as defined below.
It does not amend, replace or weaken the Main Licence, which continues to govern
every other use of the teamknitt software.

By exercising a permission under this Skill Licence, you accept its terms as
binding obligations and conditions of that permission. Rights you have
independently under applicable law are unaffected.

2. Definitions

"Skill" means the material in the skills/teamknitt directory of the teamknitt
repository as offered by the licensor under this Skill Licence: the skill
instructions (SKILL.md), reference documents, helper scripts and any other files
in that directory, together with the Bundled Runtime.

"Bundled Runtime" means the copy of the teamknitt software that the Skill
contains, or that the Skill's instructions install from the licensor's teamknitt
repository or from an official teamknitt package published by the licensor.

"Anthropic" means Anthropic, PBC and its affiliates.

"Claude" means the AI models and assistant products that Anthropic offers under
the Claude name, including the Claude apps, Claude Code, and Claude models
accessed through Anthropic's API or through a platform that Anthropic has
authorized to offer Claude. No other assistant, agent, model or product is
Claude for this Skill Licence, even if it can load skills in the same format.

"Skill Use" means:
(a) installing or enabling the unmodified Skill in Claude;
(b) having Claude read the Skill and, at a person's direction, install and run
    the Bundled Runtime to configure, check, plan, view, demonstrate, run,
    observe and intervene in agent teams; and
(c) using the Bundled Runtime's own commands directly on workspaces that were
    created or are being worked on through (a) and (b).

Skill Use concerns the assistant that loads and operates the Skill. This Skill
Licence does not restrict which model service you choose for the agent teams
that the Bundled Runtime runs.

"You" means any individual or organization exercising permissions under this
Skill Licence, including a company, a research institution, a public body or a
nonprofit, anywhere in the world.

