Skill for Skill Use, for any purpose. This includes Commercial Use and Research
Use as the Main Licence defines them. No eligibility test, registration, request
or licence fee applies to Skill Use.

4. Sharing the Skill

You may share complete, unmodified copies of the Skill with others for their own
Skill Use, including by sending the packaged skill, sharing it inside an
organization through Claude's skill-sharing features, or publishing it in a
skill directory operated by Anthropic, provided that:
(a) each copy includes this Skill Licence and the Main Licence (LICENSE and
    LICENSING.md) and retains the copyright, author, attribution and third-party
    notices; and
(b) you do not charge a licence fee for the Skill itself.

Anthropic may host, store, display and transmit the unmodified Skill as needed
to operate those features for its users.

Each recipient receives permission for Skill Use directly from the licensor under
this Skill Licence.

5. No changes to the Skill

The Skill is offered for use as published by the licensor. Without the
licensor's prior written permission, you may not:
(a) modify, adapt, translate, shorten, extend or rewrite the Skill, including
    its instructions, reference documents and helper scripts;
(b) create another skill, prompt, plugin or instruction set derived from the
    Skill; or
(c) share or publish a changed copy of the Skill, or present any changed copy as
    the teamknitt skill.

Creating and editing your own workspaces is not a change to the Skill. You remain
free to choose and edit your own briefs, team configurations, budgets and other
workspace files that the Bundled Runtime creates for you.

You may propose changes to the licensor through the teamknitt repository. A
proposal, or its acknowledgement, gives no right to use or share a changed
Skill.

6. What this Skill Licence does not cover

Everything outside Skill Use remains governed by the Main Licence, or needs a
separate written licence from the licensor. In particular, this Skill Licence
does not permit you to:
(a) install, use, adapt or port the Skill in or for any assistant, agent, model
    or product other than Claude;
(b) modify the Bundled Runtime, or share a modified Bundled Runtime, except as
    the Main Licence allows;
(c) take the Bundled Runtime or any other teamknitt code out of the Skill to use
    it apart from Skill Use, or to include it in another product, package,
    service or skill;
(d) sell or commercially license the Skill or the teamknitt software, or offer
    the functionality of the teamknitt software to third parties as a hosted or
    managed service; or
(e) use any other material in the teamknitt repository that is not part of the
    Skill.

Using the Skill in Claude in the course of your own work, including paid,
business or research work, is Skill Use and is permitted. A wrapper, label or
installation method chosen mainly to obtain rights for a use described in (a) to
(e) is not Skill Use.

